run_reseact_adjoint.jl -- simulation gradient demonstration
===========================================================================
  mode          : adjoint
  grid          : 6x6x8   (production is 13x7x72 -- see the blockers in this file's header)
  window        : 3 macro steps
  objective     : SuperFast.O3:surf
  clamp_nonneg  : OFF (blocker 1)
  base point    : jittered 1e-1 relative (PPM limiter; see header)

  NOTE This demonstrates d(objective)/d(parameters) over a SHORT window on
       a SMALL grid. It is not a week of CONUS, and the header of this file
       says precisely what stands between the two.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISCRETE ADJOINT (Phase 4) -- ALL 49 parameters in ONE backward sweep,
at a cost independent of the parameter count. Stages:
  fwd    forward pass, checkpointing (u, t, dt, forcing epoch) per macro
         step and recording the accepted (t, dt) sequence
  adj    backward sweep: chemistry VJP then transport VJP per macro step
         (the adjoint of a composition reverses it)
  ref    forward-mode reference over the SAME frozen step sequence, plus
         the per-step dot-product identity <lam,Jv> == <J'lam,v>
  fdtape central differences of the frozen-dt composed map, through the
         SAME compiled programs -- the confounder-free acceptance test
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
